infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Native button vs clickable div
  desc Native ships the contract free; a div forces five hand-built obligations
  compares
    - label Native button ships the contract
      children
        - label Implicit role of button
          desc Announced as a control, for free
        - label Accessible name from content
          desc Computes its name from inner text
        - label In the sequential tab order
          desc Keyboard and switch users reach it
        - label Enter and Space activate it
          desc And Space-scroll is suppressed
        - label Disabled state and focus ring
          desc Built in, AT-tested for two decades
    - label Clickable div needs five obligations
      children
        - label role=button
          desc Else a nameless generic node
        - label tabIndex of 0
          desc Else the keyboard never arrives
        - label onKeyDown for Enter and Space
          desc Plus prevent Space from scrolling
        - label aria-disabled
          desc And actually block the handler
        - label A visible focus style
          desc Each forgettable, silent for mouse
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
